<h2 id="find-replace">Find and revise longer articles</h2>
<ol><li>Choose Find &amp; replace beside the article formatting tools. Enter a literal word or phrase, up to 200 characters.</li><li>Use Next match or Previous match to select an exact occurrence in the article. Navigation wraps. Enter in Find text selects the next match; Shift+Enter selects the previous one.</li><li>Set Match uppercase and lowercase exactly when needed. Otherwise matching ignores case using the browser's Unicode rules; it does not apply language-specific spelling or normalization.</li><li>Enter replacement text, up to 500 characters. It is literal: punctuation and dollar signs have no special meaning. Leaving it empty deletes matching text.</li><li>Choose Replace selected match for the currently selected occurrence, or Preview replace all to inspect the change count, final article length, and up to five changed passages. Apply replace all requires confirmation.</li><li>Review the changed article and any Markdown, code, or web addresses before approving an export. Replacements affect substrings throughout the article body; source notes, review notes, title, and other page details are kept.</li></ol>
<p>Searching and previewing keep writing and approval unchanged. A replacement keeps the previous workspace under Revisions in this tab and clears approval. A result over 60,000 characters is rejected before replacement. If the current workspace cannot be checkpointed, the replacement is blocked. The history is still bounded, so download a private backup to keep important versions beyond this tab.</p>
<p>Editing the article, query, case option, or replacement clears an outdated bulk preview. Query and replacement settings and excerpts are temporary, excluded from backup files and article exports, and cleared when importing/restoring a workspace or clearing the writing desk. Applied article text is kept in the normal draft. This tool does not verify facts or link destinations, call AI, or upload writing.</p>
